2:T5ba,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest way to renovate a kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A commonly lower-cost approach is to keep the existing layout and sound cabinet carcasses where suitable. Replacing doors, handles, worktops, lighting, paint and selected splashback areas can refresh the room without paying for a full replacement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where should I not cut costs in a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Avoid compromising on accurate measuring, cabinet levelling, worktop support, waterproof sealing, plumbing or electrical installation. Problems in these areas can cause damage or lead to remedial work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to fit a kitchen yourself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"DIY fitting may reduce labour costs, but mistakes with measurements, units, worktops, plumbing or electrics can remove the saving. A professional fitter can also coordinate multiple stages and help identify issues before materials are ordered."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I make a budget kitchen look more expensive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use a restrained colour scheme, align cabinet doors carefully, choose consistent handles, finish joints neatly and invest in good lighting. Preparation and installation quality can have a strong visual impact."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-ideas-on-a-budget","d"]
